name c01m02-party-crashing
timeout 700
time 1996-03-20T08:00:00Z

# F-22 LIGHTNING II (NovaLogic 1996), CAMPAIGN ONE, SORTIE 1.2 OF 8 — "PARTY CRASHING".
# Spec: mods/f22/doc/campaign.md 2. Geometry: mods/f22/doc/terrain.md 3. Substitutions:
# mods/f22/doc/substitutions.md. THE FIVE CAMPAIGN-WIDE DISCLOSURES (no F-22, 60/60 instead of
# 100/100, real ground that masks no detection, [SET] date + [DERIV] clock, unproven north) are stated in
# c01m01-snake-eyes.fbm and are NOT repeated here.
#
# THE TASK [TXT]: bomb the assembly house at Objective Talbot, briefed 45 NM NE, measured 45.6 NM on
# bearing 39.4 deg [ORF]. Chang is in session with his generals.
#
# OBJECTIVE TALBOT IS TWO DIFFERENT PLACES AND THIS FILE TAKES THE NEAR ONE (campaign.md 6). The game
# issues the codename twice — an assembly house at 45.6 NM/39.4 deg here, a command centre at
# 87.0 NM/17.6 deg in sortie 1.8, 88.3 km apart. Kept as found: this is Talbot-the-house, 1.8 is
# Talbot-the-command-centre, and the two are not merged.
#
# SUBSTITUTIONS IN THIS FILE
#   assembly house -> `target_soft`. An unhardened building is exactly the fragility class the
#     catalogue's soft row describes (a Mk-84 near miss finishes it out to tens of metres).
#   MiG-27 CAP -> `mig23`, as in 1.1 and for the reason given there.
#   SA-2 -> `sa2`. EXACT: the S-75 is in the site catalogue with its own envelope, and this is the
#     first of the three campaign-one SAM missions (1.2, 1.7, 1.8) [ORF].
#   AAA (unspecified in the .ORF beyond `ARTEMIS`/`VTNM_04`) -> `zsu23`.
#   "unspecified count of SAM sites" [TXT] -> ONE. The .ORF loads one `SA2` model and the count is not
#     in any source read; inventing a belt would be inventing the mission.
#
# WHY THE RUN-IN IS AT 3 000 m AND THAT IS THE MISSION'S ONE REAL DECISION. The S-75's engagement floor
# in this tree is 450 m and its minimum range 8 km (`core/FBSite.h`, kSa2). A laydown at 240 m — which
# is what every W2 strike in mods/f16 flies — would pass UNDER the SA-2 and the file's own reading rule
# ("an SA-2 that never launches is an engine defect") could never be tested, because a silent launcher
# would then be correct behaviour. 3 000 m puts the package inside the envelope on purpose.
# THE PRICE IS THE AAA: the ZSU-23-4's ceiling is 1 500 m, so at 3 000 m it is present and silent BY
# GEOMETRY. That is a consequence of the declared altitude, not an omission, and it is why the AAA is
# in the file at all — a gun that cannot reach is a measurement, an absent gun is a gap.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `s2lead`'s UNIT_RESULT.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 = `s2hous` reads destroyed and Storm Leader is combat-effective at the end.
#   Dying to the SA-2 on ingress or egress is a MISSION LOSS (exit 1 on s2lead), not an engine defect.
#   AN SA-2 THAT NEVER LAUNCHES IS AN ENGINE DEFECT AND MUST BE READ AS ONE — the check is mechanical:
#   `events.log` must carry `site` lines for `s2sam` (acquisition, then a release). If the package
#   flies through 8-30 km slant range inside 450-25 000 m of altitude and the launcher stays silent,
#   report that, do not re-read it as a good outcome.
#   `s2esc`'s `kill unit s2mig` is COVERAGE, not the mission: without it the MiG's death would be
#   nobody's declared objective and the run would end CRASH/exit 2 on a kill the mission wanted.
#   exit 2 = a HOSTILE aircraft died that nobody declared, or an airframe departed controlled flight
#   with nobody having shot it. It is an ENGINE finding either way. It is NOT what a friendly loss
#   looks like: a friendly with `survive` fails DECISIVELY, which ends the run before its wreck can
#   reach the ground, and that reads exit 1 (measured four times over in this campaign).

# MEASURED (exit 3, real ground): THE HOUSE FALLS AND THE SA-2 SHOOTS. The sortie succeeds by its own
# reading rule.
#   t = 77.3 s          `s2sam` SEARCH -> TRACK, firm track at 29 885 m inside the envelope (29 946 m
#                       over the old flat plane — the site stands on 692 m of ground, so the slant
#                       range to a 3 000 m target is 61 m shorter. That is the whole first-order
#                       effect of terrain on a SAM in this tree)
#   t = 108.2-151.5 s   SIX v-750 away in two salvoes of three at the SAME six timestamps as over the
#                       plane; magazine empty, `site DEPLETED`, GO_DARK, then RADIATE again on
#                       `emcon free`. ALL SIX MISS. The launcher is NOT silent, which is what the
#                       reading rule demanded be checked
#   t = 236.0 s         `s2lead` releases one mk84, CCRP, predicted miss 47.1 m, `planeM = 347.419`
#   t = 260.8 s         `damage KILL unit=s2hous reason="structure destroyed"`
#   verdict             `s2lead` SUCCESS, `s2esc` TIMEOUT, exit 3 — the same verdict the flat run gave
#   THE CCRP PLANE IS THE RELEASE POINT'S GROUND AND NOT THE TARGET'S (`FBF16Module.cpp`:
#   `SetSteerpoint(..., GroundAslM)`, and its comment says so). Here that is 347 m against the house's
#   319 m — a 28 m plane error, absorbed. 1.8 is where the same mechanism costs the target: 322 m.
#   `s2aaa` never fires, as the header predicted: 3 000 m is twice the ZSU-23-4's ceiling.

unit s2lead
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight storm2 1
  spawn 19.00053 100.49597 3000 39.4 450      # 60 km short of Talbot, on the measured run-in bearing
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off                            # a striker does not radiate
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 19.41702 100.85826 3000 450              # THE AIM POINT: the assembly house
  wp 19.59056 101.00948 3000 450              # egress 25 km beyond, straight through
  objective kill unit s2hous
  objective survive

unit s2esc
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight storm2 2
  spawn 18.99198 100.50699 3000 39.4 450      # 1.5 km across track from the striker
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim120
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 19.72939 101.13057 3000 480              # toward the CAP's scramble point, i.e. into the threat
  objective kill unit s2mig
  objective protect unit s2lead
  objective survive

unit s2mig
  module mig23
  team hostile
  spawn 19.72939 101.13057 4000 219.4 450     # 45 km beyond the house, inbound down the raid's track
  set gear up
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 219 45 3000
  set store 1 r24r
  set store 2 r24r
  set brief_master_arm arm
  wp 19.00053 100.49597 4000 450
  objective survive

unit s2hous
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 19.41702 100.85826 ground 39.4 0      # Objective Talbot, the assembly house

unit s2sam
  module sa2
  team hostile
  spawn 19.33372 100.78573 ground 39.4 0      # 12 km short of the house, ON the run-in
  set alert ready
  set emcon free

unit s2aaa
  module zsu23
  team hostile
  spawn 19.41531 100.86046 ground 39.4 0      # 300 m from the house; ceiling 1 500 m, see the header
  set alert ready
  set emcon free
